{
  "coordinateSystem": "432\u00d7934 fixed phone crop pixels; t is absolute video seconds; titleY/controlsY/tabY are translations in scene coordinates",
  "sourceUrl": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2022/10147/?time=539",
  "notes": [
    "RGB/opacity are estimates from compressed video, not recovered source alpha. Approximate opacity uncertainty \u00b10.08, tab translation \u00b13 px; expanded content translation \u00b12 px.",
    "Expanded contents and ambient field translate together with card/cover drag: titleY=controlsY\u2248coverY\u2212100 while cover stays full-size through546.379s. No fade with downward drag progress. Content begins exiting below viewport, rather than fading out in place.",
    "Opening expandedOpacity is fitted primarily to pause-bar contrast. Title text may trail that fade by roughly0.05\u20130.15 effective opacity due to antialiasing/material coloration; precise alpha cannot be disentangled.",
    "Closing expandedOpacity from546.412s is visually unidentifiable once below viewport; these values are implementation-safe estimates. BackgroundOpacity after546.546 uses material gray residual at compact-row edge, since localy100 is covered by tab bar.",
    "Tab bar is above ambient/compact material but below expanded controls and shared artwork. It slides down and fades during opening. Returning close bar is already visually opaque when first visible near546.4459s.",
    "compactGray is the neutral base material before the ambient overlay. Pressed value210 begins542.208s, then normal base248 returns during expansion.",
    "Status alpha is measured against same static glyph mask, black\u2192warm white, and does not equal expandedOpacity.",
    "No native engine easing constants or input cancellation behavior can be recovered from these raster observations.",
    "Background dim estimated from unoccluded white-page medians: 253 -> 228 -> 253, independent of sheet fill. Home-indicator brightness has qualitative phase approximation; subtle OS adaptation is not fully reconstructed."
  ],
